  "result": "The file is `src/lib/rate-limit.ts`. It holds both pieces:\n\n- **How many tries each action gets:** the `RATE_LIMIT_BUCKETS` table lists an allowance for each kind of action. For password resets, `\"auth:password-reset\"` gets 5 tries, and one more comes back each minute. Any action not in the table gets the `DEFAULT_BUCKET` allowance instead.\n- **The \"out of tries\" decision:** `consumeRateLimit()` tops up the tries for the time that has passed, then sets `allowed = tokens >= cost`. When `allowed` is false, the person is out of tries. It also works out `resetAt`, which is the \"come back later\" time.\n\nThe reset action in `src/actions/auth/reset-password.ts` only calls `consumeRateLimit` and throws `RateLimitedError` when the answer is no. The decision itself isn't made there.\n\nANSWER: src/lib/rate-limit.ts",
